# Improvement Plan — researched 2026-07-19

Research pass across four fronts: FUI/command-center credibility
(Territory Studio's work on The Martian: purpose-led readouts, visual
hierarchy that leads the eye, empowering the operator), large-scale
particle techniques (GPGPU ping-pong simulation of millions of
particles, instancing, persistent GPU buffers), game-feel research
("juice" — and the repeated finding that **sound is half the
experience**; we currently ship none), and navigation UX for large 3D
information spaces (command palettes for jump-anywhere, worlds-in-
miniature preferred for overview tasks).

Measured against the current build (30 PRs: three tiers, physics
grammar, C2 chrome, contacts, badges, 60fps at 371k notes), the gaps
rank as follows. Each phase is one loop chunk, one PR, visually
verified before merge.

## Phase 1 — Sound (the missing half)
Procedural WebAudio layer, zero binary assets (matches the repo rule):
- A deep ambient space drone that subtly shifts with tier (sky = wide
  and thin, inside a system = closer and warmer).
- Interaction voices: hover tick, commit pulse whoosh, badge chime by
  tier, supernova rumble + detonation, stardust sparkle.
- `M` to mute, state persisted; muted by default only if the browser
  blocks autoplay (resume on first gesture).

## Phase 2 — Command palette
`Cmd/Ctrl+K` (and `/`): fuzzy search across projects, vaults, and
people; enter flies there through the correct tier path (sky → galaxy
→ vault). The C2 answer to "I know its name, take me there." Pure,
tested fuzzy matcher in data.ts.

## Phase 3 — Differential rotation (galaxies that breathe)
Replace rigid group spin with in-shader rotation where angular speed
falls off with radius (flat rotation curve): arms shear and wind over
time instead of rotating as a plate. uTime-driven, zero per-frame CPU;
spin-freeze inside a system becomes a uniform toggle.

## Phase 4 — Optical depth
- Tier-3 depth of field (bokeh) focused on the star system — the
  cinematic close-up the orrery earned.
- Subtle god-ray shafts from the vault star (radial post pass, cheap).
Both gated behind the existing quality bar: 60fps at company scale or
it doesn't ship.

## Phase 5 — Sector minimap (worlds-in-miniature)
Toggleable corner map (`N`): top-down 2D projection of the whole sky
with the camera frustum wedge, black holes marked, click to fly.
Research says WIM wins for overview tasks; contacts already covers
"what's near me," the minimap covers "where am I."

## Phase 6 — Access + onboarding polish
- `?` shortcuts overlay (C2-styled) listing every key.
- One-line hint under the wordmark on first load ("scroll to dive ·
  click to enter · esc to rise"), fades permanently after first enter.
- `prefers-reduced-motion`: damp flights to direct cuts, stop ambient
  spin.
- Comet trails on the 3 most recently active projects — recency
  readable at sky scale without opening anything.

## Deferred (needs user input or backend)
- Activity time-scrub / replay (wants real event history from
  Chapters).
- Touch/mobile controls (worth a dedicated pass with device testing).
- Multiplayer presence (v2 by decision).

